WEBVTT

00:00:00.362 --> 00:00:02.209
Last video ended with this question.

00:00:02.752 --> 00:00:05.220
Here's sine x, and sine two x.

00:00:05.923 --> 00:00:07.540
Picture a bike pedal going round.

00:00:08.045 --> 00:00:10.289
Its height above the axle is sine x,

00:00:10.731 --> 00:00:12.694
and if you pedal twice as fast, its

00:00:12.735 --> 00:00:14.217
height is sine two x.

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:17.469
At the origin, sine x has slope one,

00:00:17.832 --> 00:00:19.438
because cos zero is one.

00:00:20.224 --> 00:00:22.595
Sine two x leaves the origin twice as

00:00:22.676 --> 00:00:24.163
steeply, with slope two.

00:00:24.887 --> 00:00:26.172
Where does that two come from?

00:00:26.957 --> 00:00:29.047
And what happens when the inside part isn't

00:00:29.208 --> 00:00:31.539
two x, but something like x squared?

00:00:32.124 --> 00:00:33.339
You've met the reason before.

00:00:34.063 --> 00:00:36.931
Sine two x is the sine curve squashed

00:00:37.092 --> 00:00:38.255
sideways by a half,

00:00:38.837 --> 00:00:41.725
so every slope, at matching points, doubles.

00:00:42.488 --> 00:00:44.255
The chain rule from Year 11 says the

00:00:44.296 --> 00:00:44.696
same thing.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:48.069
Two x is the inside part, the expression

00:00:48.209 --> 00:00:50.618
sine is applied to, and sine is the

00:00:50.778 --> 00:00:51.179
outside.

00:00:51.863 --> 00:00:54.208
Differentiate the outside, and keep the inside as

00:00:54.509 --> 00:00:56.153
it is: cos two x.

00:00:56.816 --> 00:00:59.731
Then multiply by the inside part's derivative, which

00:00:59.813 --> 00:01:00.214
is two.

00:01:00.859 --> 00:01:03.409
So the derivative is two cos two x,

00:01:04.013 --> 00:01:05.418
and at zero, that's two.

00:01:05.867 --> 00:01:07.313
Now a harder inside:

00:01:08.017 --> 00:01:10.205
y equals sine of x squared.

00:01:10.909 --> 00:01:13.295
Its waves bunch closer and closer, like a

00:01:13.377 --> 00:01:16.345
rider pedalling faster and faster, so no single

00:01:16.426 --> 00:01:17.829
squash makes that curve.

00:01:18.573 --> 00:01:21.225
If you only differentiated the outside, you'd get

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:22.572
cos of x squared.

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:24.481
Test it against the real slopes.

00:01:25.145 --> 00:01:27.429
At x equals a half, both are about

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:29.534
point nine seven, a ratio of one.

00:01:30.678 --> 00:01:32.904
At x equals one, the real slope is

00:01:32.945 --> 00:01:35.451
about one point zero eight, but cos of

00:01:35.593 --> 00:01:37.257
one is only point five four.

00:01:37.739 --> 00:01:38.727
That's a ratio of two.

00:01:39.433 --> 00:01:41.103
At one and a half, the ratio is

00:01:41.265 --> 00:01:41.566
three.

00:01:42.392 --> 00:01:44.128
The missing factor isn't fixed.

00:01:44.593 --> 00:01:47.264
It's two x, the derivative of the inside

00:01:47.326 --> 00:01:48.450
part, x squared.

00:01:49.154 --> 00:01:51.457
That factor is how fast the crank is

00:01:51.518 --> 00:01:53.220
turning, compared with sine x:

00:01:53.862 --> 00:01:54.001
one,

00:01:54.563 --> 00:01:56.505
two, then three times as fast.

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:58.179
Why multiply?

00:01:59.005 --> 00:02:01.400
Follow a small step at x equals one.

00:02:02.105 --> 00:02:03.839
Move x by point zero one.

00:02:04.383 --> 00:02:07.331
The inside, x squared, moves about twice as

00:02:07.392 --> 00:02:10.059
far, about point zero two, because its rate

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:11.846
there is two x, which is two.

00:02:12.608 --> 00:02:14.977
Then sine reacts to its own input at

00:02:15.017 --> 00:02:17.527
a rate of cos one, about point five

00:02:17.587 --> 00:02:17.848
four.

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:21.156
So y moves about point five four times

00:02:21.257 --> 00:02:23.662
point zero two, which is about point zero

00:02:23.803 --> 00:02:24.223
one one.

00:02:24.926 --> 00:02:26.427
That's why it's called a chain:

00:02:26.969 --> 00:02:29.072
each link passes its change on to the

00:02:29.133 --> 00:02:31.056
next, multiplied by its own rate.

00:02:31.838 --> 00:02:33.644
Rates along a chain multiply:

00:02:34.208 --> 00:02:36.255
d y by d u, times d u

00:02:36.316 --> 00:02:36.938
by d x.

00:02:37.608 --> 00:02:39.776
Now plug in the outsides from this unit.

00:02:40.419 --> 00:02:42.224
For e to the power of an inside

00:02:42.265 --> 00:02:44.511
part, copy e to that power,

00:02:45.014 --> 00:02:47.260
then multiply by the power's derivative.

00:02:48.003 --> 00:02:50.025
For the natural log of an inside part,

00:02:50.447 --> 00:02:53.070
the derivative is the inside's derivative, over the

00:02:53.191 --> 00:02:54.051
inside itself,

00:02:54.693 --> 00:02:56.095
and the inside has to be positive.

00:02:56.918 --> 00:02:59.647
For sine of an inside part, it's cos

00:02:59.728 --> 00:03:02.438
of the same inside, times the inside's derivative.

00:03:03.121 --> 00:03:05.124
And for cos, it's minus sine of the

00:03:05.145 --> 00:03:07.610
same inside, times the inside's derivative.

00:03:08.293 --> 00:03:10.680
Each time, the inside stays unchanged.

00:03:11.525 --> 00:03:13.632
For instance, e to the x squared has

00:03:13.653 --> 00:03:16.062
derivative two x, times e to the x

00:03:16.083 --> 00:03:16.464
squared.

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:17.839
First example.

00:03:18.428 --> 00:03:21.416
Differentiate y equals e to the sine x.

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:24.865
The outside is e to a power, and

00:03:24.906 --> 00:03:25.787
the inside is sine x.

00:03:27.312 --> 00:03:30.016
Copy e to the sine x, then multiply

00:03:30.117 --> 00:03:32.380
by the derivative of sine x, which is

00:03:32.522 --> 00:03:32.962
cos x.

00:03:33.924 --> 00:03:36.008
So d y by d x is e

00:03:36.049 --> 00:03:38.233
to the sine x, times cos x.

00:03:39.297 --> 00:03:40.964
Now look at the graph at pi over

00:03:41.005 --> 00:03:41.205
two.

00:03:41.908 --> 00:03:44.133
Cos of pi over two is zero, so

00:03:44.235 --> 00:03:45.196
the gradient is zero.

00:03:45.919 --> 00:03:48.283
The inside, sine x, is at its peak

00:03:48.464 --> 00:03:50.748
and stops changing, so the whole curve goes

00:03:50.809 --> 00:03:51.289
flat too.

00:03:52.355 --> 00:03:53.987
Swap the order, and the answer changes.

00:03:54.653 --> 00:03:56.896
For sine of e to the x, the

00:03:56.957 --> 00:03:59.861
outside is sine, so the derivative is cos

00:04:00.063 --> 00:04:02.045
of e to the x, times e to

00:04:02.086 --> 00:04:02.406
the x.

00:04:02.901 --> 00:04:06.697
Second example: y equals the natural log of

00:04:06.817 --> 00:04:07.601
cos x.

00:04:08.443 --> 00:04:10.447
A log needs a positive input, so this

00:04:10.487 --> 00:04:13.071
curve only exists where cos x is positive,

00:04:13.532 --> 00:04:16.036
for example between minus pi over two and

00:04:16.076 --> 00:04:16.697
pi over two.

00:04:17.538 --> 00:04:19.301
The outside is the natural log,

00:04:19.803 --> 00:04:22.690
so the derivative is the inside's derivative, over

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:23.231
the inside.

00:04:23.793 --> 00:04:26.738
That's minus sine x, over cos x, which

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:27.961
is minus tan x,

00:04:28.563 --> 00:04:30.266
but only where cos x is positive.

00:04:31.128 --> 00:04:32.972
At pi over four, it's minus one,

00:04:33.515 --> 00:04:35.398
and the tangent on the graph agrees.

00:04:36.275 --> 00:04:38.342
Third example, with cos on the outside.

00:04:38.865 --> 00:04:42.215
Differentiate y equals cos of, x squared plus

00:04:42.357 --> 00:04:42.496
one.

00:04:43.259 --> 00:04:45.322
The outside is cos, so its slope is

00:04:45.423 --> 00:04:48.588
minus sine of the same inside: minus sine

00:04:48.709 --> 00:04:49.930
of, x squared plus one.

00:04:50.774 --> 00:04:53.240
The inside's derivative is two x, because the

00:04:53.361 --> 00:04:54.203
one is a constant.

00:04:55.026 --> 00:04:56.828
Multiply them, and d y by d x

00:04:57.029 --> 00:04:59.914
is minus two x, sine of, x squared

00:04:59.975 --> 00:05:00.435
plus one.

00:05:01.318 --> 00:05:03.823
At x equals one, that's minus two sine

00:05:03.864 --> 00:05:04.084
two,

00:05:04.606 --> 00:05:06.309
about minus one point eight two.

00:05:07.234 --> 00:05:09.301
Two things to keep: the minus sign from

00:05:09.322 --> 00:05:11.510
the outside, and the two x from the

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:12.012
inside.

00:05:12.575 --> 00:05:13.963
Here's a short way to say the whole

00:05:14.044 --> 00:05:14.285
rule.

00:05:14.948 --> 00:05:17.997
Outside slope at the inside, times the inside

00:05:18.058 --> 00:05:18.338
slope.

00:05:18.903 --> 00:05:20.919
The words "at the inside" matter.

00:05:21.542 --> 00:05:24.206
For sine of x squared, the outside slope

00:05:24.288 --> 00:05:26.451
is cos of x squared, not cos x,

00:05:26.873 --> 00:05:28.636
and the inside slope is two x.

00:05:29.219 --> 00:05:31.433
So the derivative is two x cos of

00:05:31.454 --> 00:05:31.997
x squared.

00:05:32.741 --> 00:05:35.026
For the natural log, keep the inside positive,

00:05:35.328 --> 00:05:37.051
and use one over it for the outside

00:05:37.092 --> 00:05:37.352
slope.

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:40.528
Your turn.

00:05:41.036 --> 00:05:44.128
Differentiate y equals the natural log of, x

00:05:44.169 --> 00:05:45.233
squared minus nine.

00:05:45.816 --> 00:05:47.603
Then state the values of x for which

00:05:47.644 --> 00:05:48.627
your answer is valid.

00:05:49.232 --> 00:05:50.064
Pause here to answer.

00:06:00.955 --> 00:06:03.762
The inside is x squared minus nine, with

00:06:03.783 --> 00:06:04.805
derivative two x.

00:06:05.429 --> 00:06:07.599
So d y by d x is two

00:06:07.741 --> 00:06:09.550
x, over x squared minus nine.

00:06:10.452 --> 00:06:12.475
The log needs x squared minus nine to

00:06:12.516 --> 00:06:14.939
be positive, so x squared is more than

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:15.280
nine:

00:06:16.062 --> 00:06:18.164
x is less than minus three, or more

00:06:18.206 --> 00:06:18.645
than three.

00:06:19.328 --> 00:06:21.694
Saying only x isn't plus or minus three

00:06:22.097 --> 00:06:22.637
isn't enough.

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:25.606
Between minus three and three, the inside is

00:06:25.727 --> 00:06:27.552
negative, and the log doesn't exist.

00:06:29.303 --> 00:06:29.686
Last one.

00:06:30.391 --> 00:06:33.259
For y equals sine of the natural log

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:35.245
of x, with x positive,

00:06:35.786 --> 00:06:37.230
find d y by d x.

00:06:37.873 --> 00:06:40.503
Then find the exact gradient at x equals

00:06:40.664 --> 00:06:40.784
e.

00:06:41.448 --> 00:06:42.212
Pause here to answer.

00:06:53.861 --> 00:06:56.476
The outside is sine, and the inside is

00:06:56.516 --> 00:06:57.502
the natural log of x.

00:06:58.044 --> 00:07:00.349
So d y by d x is cos

00:07:00.590 --> 00:07:02.694
of the natural log of x, times one

00:07:02.855 --> 00:07:03.316
over x.

00:07:04.217 --> 00:07:06.339
At x equals e, the natural log of

00:07:06.359 --> 00:07:09.342
e is one, so the gradient is cos

00:07:09.562 --> 00:07:11.924
one, over e, about point two.

00:07:12.666 --> 00:07:14.148
If you left out the one over x,

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:17.035
you'd get cos one, about point five four,

00:07:17.416 --> 00:07:19.139
and you'd have skipped the inside slope.

00:07:20.674 --> 00:07:22.595
So for any of these functions with an

00:07:22.636 --> 00:07:25.698
inside part, take the outside's slope at the

00:07:25.759 --> 00:07:26.178
inside,

00:07:26.699 --> 00:07:29.081
and multiply by the inside's slope.

00:07:29.844 --> 00:07:31.833
And for a log, keep the inside positive.

00:07:32.697 --> 00:07:32.956
Next,

00:07:33.559 --> 00:07:36.765
two functions multiplied together, like e to the

00:07:36.907 --> 00:07:38.068
x times sine x.

00:07:39.114 --> 00:07:40.950
How do both parts set the slope?

00:07:43.621 --> 00:07:44.505
Here are the key notes.

00:07:45.027 --> 00:07:46.796
Pause the video if you need more time

00:07:46.816 --> 00:07:47.298
to copy them.
